# NEXVION — Docker build context allowlist
#
# Strategy: exclude EVERYTHING first, then re-include only the NEXVION
# application source and our own build/runtime assets.
#
# Why an allowlist instead of a denylist: this repo will accumulate Terraform,
# Helm, Ansible, monitoring, docs and CI directories over the course of the
# capstone. A denylist has to be edited every time one is added, and a forgotten
# entry silently ships your IaC into the runtime layer. An allowlist fails closed.
#
# Pattern precedence is last-match-wins (same as .gitignore), which is why the
# exclusions come first and the re-inclusions after.

*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXVION application source — these 9 files are provided and must never change
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!index.html
!products.html
!payment.html
!script.js
!payment.js
!style.css
!products.css
!payment.css
!logo.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build-stage tooling + runtime web-server configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!docker
!docker/**

# NOTE: Dockerfile and .dockerignore are always sent to the daemon by `docker
# build` and cannot be excluded, so they are not listed above. They are never
# COPYed into a stage, so they never reach the final image.